{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1095315-did-the-wod-ever-have-a-supernatural-market","id":1095315,"title":"Did the WoD ever have a supernatural market?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T18:30:21-07:00","id":1095315,"title":"Did the WoD ever have a supernatural market?","content":"Has the WoD ever had some place that is a neutral ground for supernaturals where they can trade goods and services?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T18:31:53-07:00","id":1095317,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Official WoD. but nWoD fansplat Genius had the Lemurian Zoathica. Basically a walmart/masonic lodge for mad scientists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T19:33:19-07:00","id":1095332,"title":"","content":"Not that I know of in One World of Darkness. You can certainly put a fencer of supernatural artifacts in your game - maybe a static sorcerer? - but I'd keep things mysterious and uncertain about the whole operation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T19:47:04-07:00","id":1095334,"title":"","content":"In Mage there's something that's a bit like that, but it's not on the normal world.<br /> <br /> In the Digital Web (Internet realm), there's a place called the Spy's Demise, that it's a neutral ground in the Ascension War (if you start a fight, you're expelled). Not everyone can find it's way there, and it's clients are mostly mages (and mostly Technocrats and Virtual Adepts)...but anyone that can enter (like, say, the ocasional Glasswalker) it's welcomed to stay and talk to the customers. There's one human that managed to discover the place. You only need Virtual Reality gear, good directions and luck, so, a tech saavy vampire could do it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T15:58:08-07:00","id":1096889,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness had the Goblin Markets for Changeling: The Lost, but no overall marketplace thing. Classic World of Darkness didn't really have anything like that, but there were a few things that could be adapted to it.<br /> As Aleph mentioned, there is/was the Spy's Demise in Mage's Digital Web (that could be accessed via Werewolf's Cyberrealm umbral realm and by Wraiths with the Inhabit power; sadly, Changeling was always a tad technophobic, so I don't recall any computer/cyber oriented dreamscapes that might have connected to it, but you can always make your own; Vampires would probably need either Auspex combined with some sort of VR system or some sort of Thaumaturgical method, although there might be some sort of crazy arcane computer out there that allows a vampire to enter the Digital Web if you feed it Vitae).<br /> Wraith had the Midnight Express train that ran through the dead lands. Any mage or were beast able to enter the Dark Umbra could in theory ride said train. Perhaps Sluagh as well, and any Vampire that could enter the underworld.<br /> Vampire's Succubus Club - either it's original Chicago based location or the traveling rave version in Nights of Prophecy - could end up as a sort of weird neutral ground where the rules of elysium also apply to visiting Hollow Ones, fey folk, skin-ridden Mediums and the like.<br /> And then there was - sigh - the Midnight Circus, which was kind of a train wreck of goofiness. (My favorite review of it included the line, &quot;I stopped taking it seriously when I got to the trained dog act made up of Black Spiral Dancers.&quot;). Still, you might be able to salvage it by dropping about a third of the listed acts, fiddling with the rest, getting rid of the presented management and making it into this sort of nebulous place where one might be able to find what they've been wishing for, but at a price that's more than they bargained for (see Ray Bradbury's &quot;Something Wicked This Way Comes&quot;, Clive Barker's &quot;The Hellbound Heart&quot;, Charles G. Finney's &quot;The Circus of Dr. Lao&quot;, and probably three or four dozen episodes of The Twilight Zone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T00:33:26-07:00","id":1098011,"title":"","content":"My table used something similar to the neutral ground in Constantine. It was controlled by a homebrew npc that &quot;seemed&quot; ro have powers from every splat but didn't seem to be a member of any","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}